# Variant of lab_e_exp_lqr_u0.fly with VAR 47 g_xyc_delay_ticks=12 (firmware default, TASK/StabilizerTask.c:2004) instead of 21 (10-24 xy limit cycle).
# N3/4 lqr_3l u0: baseline-only control arm for E3, hover then figure-8. Flight order: lab_e_exp_pid_u0,
#   lab_e_exp_adrc_u0, lab_e_exp_lqr_u0, lab_e_exp_mpc_u0. Each is its E twin plus takeoff mrac_injection=0
#   (same exp row; MRAC runs and logs but its output is not applied, as in lab_m_memory_u0).
# Fly it: fly lab_e_exp_lqr_u0 --once at >= 15.8 V resting. UNVERIFIED: never flown.
# Purpose: E vs N isolates the adaptive layer per baseline (thesis: controller-agnostic MRAC); N's position
#   response gives each baseline's own closed-loop bw to replace the PROPOSED s_xyrm rows
#   (TASK/StabilizerTask.c:1695-1701; only PID's 2.0 rad/s is measured).
campaign lab-e-exp-lqr-3l-u0
rate 100
log velocity_loops camera_fusion
slow 50 nn4 xy_ctrl mrac_3l mrac_theta ekf_states estimator_truth thrust_model optical_flow takeoff_gate mrac_shadow
exp lqr_3l
set g_traj_ff_shift_s=0 g_land_xy_gate_cm=10 g_xyc_delay_ticks=12
takeoff 0.5 mrac_injection=0
hold 3
set traj_p.move_s=18 traj_p.ret_s=3 traj_p.hold_s=1 traj_p.profile=1 traj_p.ramp_s=2 traj_p.yaw_follow=0
preset figure8 f8_a_cm=30
hold 3
land
